<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT FALLS 2.1 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT FALLS 2.1 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian banks' internal credit</p>
<p>fell to 1,188.2 billion levs on October 4 from 1,215.7 billion</p>
<p>levs on September 27, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Credit to the government edged down 0.28 percent to 494.6</p>
<p>billion levs, credit to state firms fell 4.73 percent to 310</p>
<p>billion levs and lev-denominated credit to private firms inched</p>
<p>down 0.68 percent to 131.5 billion levs.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE     OCT 4-SEPT27  SEPT27-AUG30 AUG30-JULY26</p>
<p> Total internal credit	 -2.13	 +6.57	  +4.70</p>
<p> Credit to govt		  -0.28	 +4.75	  +2.98</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	 -4.73	 +7.39	  +5.91</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms -0.68	 +1.30	  +2.43</p>
<p> NOMINAL (BILLION LEVS)	 OCT 4     SEPT 27	AUG 30</p>
<p> Total internal credit	1,188.2     1,214.1     1,139.2</p>
<p> Credit to govt		   494.6	 496.0	 473.5</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	  310.0	 325.4	 303.0</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms  131.5	 132.4	 130.7</p>
<p>Dlr credit to private firms</p>
<p> (USD billion)		     $1.14	 $1.13	 $1.15</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
